OL,3,AHousehold energy bills to hit
OL,4,Athree-year high as Ofgem announces 4%
OL,5,Arise from October
OL,6,
OL,7,FEnergy prices for millions of
OL,8,Fhouseholds will rise to the highest
OL,9,Flevel for three years, under regulator
OL,10,FOfgem's price cap.
OL,12,FThe cap reflects the rise in the
OL,13,Fwholesale cost of gas, paid by
OL,14,Fsuppliers, but will hit household bills
OL,15,Fjust as the colder weather arrives in
OL,16,FOctober.
OL,18,FOfgem said the price cap will increase
OL,19,Fby 4% compared with the current level,
OL,20,Fwith a household using a typical amount
OL,21,Fof gas and electricity paying #60 a
OL,22,Fyear more.
OL,23,APub: 25-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  BusinessC Nat TVF  Nat News
